WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:05.899
Speaking on Ukrainian state television, President
Petro Poroshenko said he turned to Berlin

00:00:05.899 --> 00:00:10.900
after the Kremlin failed to respond to his
request for dialogue.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:20.650
"Immediately at night, I ordered a phone conversation
with the President of Russia Putin.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:27.190
We did not receive response and I had to address
to the German Chancellor so that she can talk

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:34.430
to Putin on immediate release of Ukrainian
servicemen and Ukrainian ships."

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:39.520
Poroshenko also said the authorities would
take all necessary steps to release the Ukrainian

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:45.030
sailors detained on Sunday when Russia seized
three vessels off the Crimean coast.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:49.470
Captured sailors appeared in a Russian court,
and were charged with unlawfully entering

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.420
the country, carrying weapons.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:56.760
They face up to six years in jail.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:01.469
Earlier other sailors were shown on Russian
television, saying they had deliberately entered

00:01:01.469 --> 00:01:03.969
Russian waters as a provocation.

00:01:03.969 --> 00:01:08.240
Kiev denounced what it described as forced
confessions

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:16.930
Moscow accuses Kyiv of sparking the sea skirmish
to boost support ahead of an election.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:21.740
Most probably this provocation took place
in order to achieve certain political decisions

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:28.799
which are beneficial for the current President
of Ukraine."

00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:34.240
Ukraine accuses Russia of illegally capturing
its ships and sailors off the coast of Crimea.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:39.470
President Petro Poroshenko now claims Moscow
is preparing for an invasion.

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:43.280
Together with the country's parliament, he
has imposed martial law in the regions bordering

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:46.570
Russia for 30 days.

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:57.189
"Fundamentally the whole martial law is about
getting resources together and for everybody

00:01:57.189 --> 00:02:04.950
here in Ukraine to understand his or her place
when the Russians come further."

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:09.769
President Poroshenko insisted the measures
won't interfere with elections scheduled for

00:02:09.769 --> 00:02:10.769
March.

00:02:10.769 --> 00:02:16.650
But his decree is causing concern and confusion
in the capital Kyiv.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:20.950
For Ukrainians, it's unclear what changes
martial law will bring.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:04:13.180
After a four-year stand-off with Russia, peace
seems

00:04:13.180 --> 00:05:18.469
a distant outcome.

